export anchor ControlPanelStyle:
    number: 44
    screen: Settings
    name: Control panel
    idea: Settings laid out like an industrial equipment panel in light brushed metal, with rocker switches, engraved labels, rivets and shaped indicator lamps.
    base: light
    palette:
        housing: #c3c8cd, the page behind the plates with faint horizontal lines
        plate: #dde0e3, brushed module plates as a gradient from #e5e8eb to #d5d9dd with fine vertical streaks
        plateHigh: #eceef0, the nameplate tag, raised keys and demo rows
        edge: #8a9198, borders on plates, keys and tab buttons
        engrave: #2b3035, labels, body text and the primary button
        label: #454c53, secondary engraving and the OFF lamp word
        lampOn: #155f29, the round lit ON lamp and its word
        pointerAmber: #9a5b00, the triangle above the selected tab and the selected digest key
        lcd: #cdd5c0, readout windows and the saved status, with ink #1e2a14
        danger: #a3221b, the Leave workspace button
        hazard: #f2c400, the danger stripe band in diagonals with #1f2326, decoration only
        focus: #0b57d0, the focus outline
    type:
        A condensed technical sans, Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, D-DIN, Roboto
        Condensed, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif. The page title is 26px
        bold in capitals with 0.06em tracking. The brand is 22px bold
        capitals with wide 0.28em tracking. Engraved labels are 12px bold
        capitals with 0.12em tracking and a white 1px text shadow below.
        Row text is 15px semibold, hints 13px regular. Readouts and lamp
        words use Consolas, Menlo or another monospace, 18px bold in the
        readout and 12px bold beside lamps.
    layout:
        A nameplate plate across the top with the brand, a small Settings
        tag and Operator Mara Okafor on the right. Next a plate with the
        Settings title and five tab push buttons in a row. Below, a grid
        with a wide Notifications plate on the left and a narrower stack on
        the right holding Time and language, a Commit plate with the
        buttons and saved readout, and the Danger zone plate. Under 860px
        everything stacks, and under 520px the tab buttons wrap three to a
        row.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between plates, 24px plate padding, 14px vertical padding on each row.
    density: Medium. One control per row with a groove line between rows.
    corners: 6px plates, 4px keys, rockers and buttons, 3px fields and readout windows.
    borders:
        1px #8a9198 on every metal part. Section titles run into a groove
        made of a dark line over a light line. Each plate has a small
        domed rivet in all four corners.
    shadows:
        Raised parts carry a solid 3px bottom edge in a darker grey and a
        white inner top highlight. Pressed parts drop 2px and use an inset
        shadow. Readouts and fields are recessed with an inset shadow.
    icons:
        Indicator lamps carry meaning by shape. A round glowing lamp with
        the word ON means on, a hollow square with the word OFF means off.
        A solid amber triangle marks the selected tab and digest key while
        other keys show a hollow circle. Saved shows a filled circle tick.
        The danger zone shows a yellow warning triangle and a door exit
        icon on its button. Switches are two-half rockers printed On and
        Off, with the active half raised and pale.
    focus: A 3px #0b57d0 outline offset 3px around the button, rocker, key or field.
    tone: Terse panel labels in capitals, such as Operator, Commit and Changes saved.
